WEBVTT

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:05.456
Hi, I'm Hellen for Openline.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.168
Let's set up your eSIM.

00:00:07.648 --> 00:00:09.856
Use an unlocked, compatible phone

00:00:09.856 --> 00:00:12.528
and Wi-Fi. Redeem any purchase

00:00:12.528 --> 00:00:14.112
code first; it's not

00:00:14.112 --> 00:00:15.712
the eSIM activation code.

00:00:16.168 --> 00:00:17.296
Choose QR or manual

00:00:17.296 --> 00:00:18.672
entry, not both.

00:00:19.136 --> 00:00:20.784
Show your QR on another

00:00:20.784 --> 00:00:23.504
screen. On iPhone, open Settings,

00:00:24.064 --> 00:00:25.520
then Cellular or Mobile Data.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.824
Tap Add eSIM, then the

00:00:27.824 --> 00:00:29.280
QR option if shown.

00:00:29.632 --> 00:00:31.824
Scan, confirm the prompts, and

00:00:31.824 --> 00:00:32.928
wait for setup to finish.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.536
For manual entry instead, on

00:00:35.536 --> 00:00:37.456
that QR screen tap Enter

00:00:37.456 --> 00:00:39.696
Details Manually. Paste your supplied

00:00:39.696 --> 00:00:42.400
SM-DP+ address and activation code

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.880
exactly, with no extra spaces.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.136
Add a confirmation code only

00:00:47.136 --> 00:00:49.280
if supplied. Tap Next and

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:50.448
follow the setup prompts.

00:00:51.152 --> 00:00:52.896
These examples aren't valid codes.

00:00:53.392 --> 00:00:55.504
iOS twenty-six may ask travel

00:00:55.504 --> 00:00:58.160
questions. If asked, choose Abroad

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.192
for international travel, and Data

00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:01.680
Only if your plan matches.

00:01:02.144 --> 00:01:03.824
In mobile settings, select the

00:01:03.824 --> 00:01:05.808
new line, then Cellular Plan

00:01:05.808 --> 00:01:07.776
Label. Name it Openline.

00:01:07.984 --> 00:01:09.392
If keeping your home number,

00:01:09.392 --> 00:01:11.872
use Primary for calls, texts,

00:01:12.512 --> 00:01:13.888
iMessage and FaceTime.

00:01:14.352 --> 00:01:15.472
Home calls and texts

00:01:15.472 --> 00:01:17.168
may incur roaming charges.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.536
Follow your plan's activation and

00:01:19.536 --> 00:01:21.152
validity rules. When ready to

00:01:21.152 --> 00:01:23.488
use it, turn Openline on.

00:01:24.048 --> 00:01:25.856
Select it for Cellular Data.

00:01:26.384 --> 00:01:28.784
Turn Allow Cellular Data Switching off.

00:01:29.424 --> 00:01:31.424
Turn Openline Data Roaming on

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:32.832
if your plan says to.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.184
Keep home Data Roaming off.

00:01:35.824 --> 00:01:37.408
Don't need regular calls or

00:01:37.408 --> 00:01:39.296
texts? You can turn the

00:01:39.296 --> 00:01:40.144
home line off.

00:01:40.528 --> 00:01:41.600
That's not deleting it.

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:43.416
Turn Wi-Fi off and open

00:01:43.416 --> 00:01:44.712
a webpage to test internet

00:01:44.712 --> 00:01:46.744
access, not just check bars.

00:01:47.224 --> 00:01:48.720
Recheck data and roaming if

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.832
needed. Contact Openline support

00:01:50.832 --> 00:01:52.648
before deleting your eSIM.

00:01:52.928 --> 00:01:54.728
Android uses QR or manual

00:01:54.728 --> 00:01:56.288
too, with different menus.

00:01:56.784 --> 00:01:59.664
On Samsung, try Settings, Connections,

00:02:00.096 --> 00:02:01.856
SIM manager, Add eSIM.

00:02:01.856 --> 00:02:05.080
On Pixel, Settings, Network and

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:07.576
internet, SIMs, Add SIM.

00:02:08.184 --> 00:02:10.152
Choose Openline for data and

00:02:10.152 --> 00:02:11.808
follow your plan's roaming rules.

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.944
Your checklist: one installation method,

00:02:15.408 --> 00:02:16.832
the right data line, and

00:02:16.832 --> 00:02:17.696
a connection test.

00:02:18.144 --> 00:02:19.688
Find the guide at Openline

00:02:19.688 --> 00:02:21.360
dot com slash install.

00:02:21.904 --> 00:02:22.720
Enjoy your travels!
